I tried on my project and i writed 
```
`export default async function Home() {
  const res = await fetch("http://localhost:3000/api/test");
  console.log(res.ok);

  // const params = useParams();
  return (
    <div className="m-auto flex  flex-col items-start justify-start gap-y-16 pb-10 xl:mt-16">
    </div>
  );
}`
```

and i defined
 ```
// /app/api/test/route.ts

export async function GET() {
  return Response.json({ data: { message: "Hello World!" } });
}
```

And i execute npm run build, i have no error. The only way where u can have an error "ECONNREFUSED" is that you fetch a undefined route

I fixed it by using the route handler in client components only, and using a separate async fetch in server components. @Bahlaouane-Hamza is right in giving this advice as it indeed does prevent another 'round-trip'. But of course the issue still persists. I still can't use route handlers in servers components.

@devajakamerus  `next dev` has no issues. The error occurs when I try to build. I tried `"build": "NODE_OPTIONS='--dns-result-order=ipv4first' next build"`, but no luck there either.

